    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0085" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg1"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.712/69</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Postmaster General</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Burleson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received May 16.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to this Department’s letter of
                    the 9th ultimo,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1-f1"/> transmitting a copy of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Daily Bulletin</hi> of this Department containing the
                    Postmaster General’s Order No. 211 of the 7th ultimo,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1-f2"/> suspending mail service for and via Germany, I have the
                    honor to transmit herewith for the information of your Department a copy of the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Daily Bulletin</hi> of the Department containing the
                    Postmaster General’s Order No. 331 of today’s date,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1-f3"
                    /> giving notice that the provisions of Order No. 211 are not to be understood
                    as applying to mail for or from prisoners of war.</p>
                <p>By direction of the Postmaster General:</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. A. Fisher</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Second Assistant Postmaster General</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
